# <Study> — <topic> (TVBO replication)

**Replication** of <Author> et al., *<title>*, <venue> (<Year>). One declarative recipe
(`<Study>.yaml`) + minimal plotting; a *replication*, not a bit-exact reproduction (see
the report's scorecard). Backend chosen by fit — see `report/analysis/backend-fit.md`.

## Layout (FAIR)
```
<Study>/
  <Study>.yaml              THE spec — one declarative recipe at the root (all/selected experiments)
  README.md  environment.yml / requirements.txt
  code/                     ALL code, FLAT (the spec stays OUT of code/); importable with no config
    <study>_networks.py  <study>_analysis.py  <study>_figures.py   callables the spec references (module: / code_modules:)
    prepare_<study>.py  <study>_reference.py (verify)
  input/
    DATA.md                 TRACKED — provenance + exact download/regenerate steps
    sourcedata/             third-party raw inputs (connectomes, …) — git-ignored
  figures/                  rendered figures + their generated plot_<name>.py — git-ignored
  output/                   run outputs (git-ignored): result .h5 containers, KPI tables, report.pdf
  report/                   ALL of OUR work (tracked): report.qmd (whole report) + report_internal.qmd (A/B wrapper) + _quarto.yml + references.bib   (*.pdf git-ignored)
    analysis/               OUR replication analysis (tracked): targets.md, figures.md, backend-fit.md, adherence.md
  original_study/           the PAPER's own material ONLY — fully git-ignored, obtained per DATA.md
    <paper.pdf>  img/fig*.png  source_data/  <pristine paper code>
```
## Reproduce
```bash
python code/prepare_<study>.py            # (only if the study has external inputs) raw source -> tvbo-ready Network
tvbo run <Study>.yaml                      # all experiments in dependency order, THEN renders figures/ (--experiment for a subset; --no-figures to skip)
tvbo figure render <Study>.yaml           # (re-render figures only, without re-running experiments)
cd report && quarto render                 # ONE command -> BOTH report.pdf (public; shareable) AND report_internal.pdf (A/B; local-only)
```
The report is ONE Quarto project: `report.qmd` (the whole report) + `report_internal.qmd` (a thin
`{{< include report.qmd >}}` wrapper) + `_quarto.yml`. `quarto render` (no file arg) builds both
PDFs in one pass; do NOT pass `--to pdf` (that forces xelatex — `_quarto.yml` already sets `typst`).
